{
    "background_story": "Tommy Townes was a free-spirited musician who traveled from town to town, sharing his soulful melodies with anyone who would listen. With his trusty guitar by his side, he'd play on street corners, in local cafes, and at town festivals. His music was a reflection of the people and places he encountered, weaving stories of love, heartache, and everyday life. As he wandered, Tommy collected tales and inspirations, which he'd later craft into songs that resonated deeply with his audiences. His nomadic lifestyle earned him the nickname 'The Townes Troubadour,' and though he never stayed in one place for long, his music left a lasting impact on the hearts of those who heard him play.",
